<title>UK: NWE straight-run fuel eases, Greece tenders to buy.</title>
<headline>NWE straight-run fuel eases, Greece tenders to buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil was steady to weaker on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>Greece issued a tender to buy one 20,000 tonne straight-run cargo with a maximum sulphur content of 0.35 percent, and an optional 20,000 tonne cargo in April or May.</p>
<p>One player said he was offering North Sea barrels for late February at around $122 fob NWE. Buyers were scarce, however.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
